  <paragraphs xml:id="description">
    <title>Course Description</title>
    <p>
      Limits, continuity, derivatives and integrals of functions of one variable including polynomial, root, rational, exponential, logarithmic, trigonometric, and inverse trigonometric functions. Applications of calculus are included. 
    </p>
    <p>
      Prerequisites: Math 121 (minimum grade of C-) OR computed math placement score MA221
    </p>
  </paragraphs>

  <paragraphs xml:id="instructional-format">
    <title>Instructional Format</title>
    <p>This is a face-to-face course, which means we will meet in person.</p>
  </paragraphs>

  <paragraphs xml:id="course-materials">
    <title>Course Materials</title>
    <p>
      Required Text:  Calculus: 8th Edition by Hughes-Hallett, Gleason, McCallum et al., ISBN: 978-1-119-77780-9.  This text is recommended.  
    </p>
  </paragraphs>

